================================================================
  musil: language reference
================================================================

--- variables and arithmetic ---
x = 10 y = 3
x + y = 13
x - y = 7
x * y = 30
x / y = 3.33333333333333
(- 7) (unary) = -7
abs (- 7) = 7
mod 17 5 = 2

--- comparisons and booleans ---
x < y : 0
x > y : 1
x == 10: 1
x != y : 1
and 1 1: 1
or  0 1: 1
not 0  : 1
min: 1
max: 9

--- expr Pratt: infix math ---
x + y * 2     = 16
(x + y) * 2   = 26
(+ x y) * 2   = 26
x % y         = 1
(inc x) + y * 2 = 17

--- math functions ---
sqrt 2     : 1.4142135623731
sin pi/2   : 1
cos 0      : 1
tan pi/4   : 1
exp 1      : 2.71828182845905
log e      : 1
floor 3.7  : 3
ceil  3.2  : 4
round 3.5  : 4

--- vectors and broadcast ---
v          : (1 2 3 4 5)
v + 10     : (11 12 13 14 15)
v * 2      : (2 4 6 8 10)
v + v      : (2 4 6 8 10)
sin v      : (0.841470984807897 0.909297426825682 0.141120008059867 -0.756802495307928 -0.958924274663138)
range 5      : (0 1 2 3 4)
linspace 0 1 5: (0 0.25 0.5 0.75 1)
zeros 4      : (0 0 0 0)
ones 3       : (1 1 1)
sum v        : 15
mean v       : 3
sort         : (1 1 2 3 4 5 6 9)

--- lists ---
L            : (1 two 3 (4 5))
list 1 2 3   : (1 2 3)
cons 0 ...   : (0 1 2 3)
append       : (1 2 3 4)
after push 99: (10 20 30 99)
popped       : 99
after pop    : (10 20 30)

--- polymorphic ops (LIST, NUM, STR) ---
length list: 3   vec: 3   str: 5
head   list: 10   vec: 10
tail   list: (20 30)   vec: (20 30)
empty? ()  : 1   empty? L: 0
getidx vec : 30
getidx str : e
vc after setidx: (999 20 30)

--- higher-order (polymorphic on list and vec) ---
map sqr list: (1 4 9 16)
map sqr vec : (1 4 9 16)
filter list : (2 4 6)
filter vec  : (4 5 6)
reduce sum  : 15
reduce prod : 120

--- strings ---
concat   : hello, world! 42
split    : (a b c d)
join     : x-y-z
upper    : MUSIL
lower    : musil
trim     : [hi]

--- control flow ---
x > 5: yes
x is normal
while: sum 0..9 = 45
for:   sum 0..9 = 45
break at j = 7
odds 1..10 : (1 3 5 7 9)

--- functions ---
square 7: 49
2x^2 + 3x + 1 at x=4: 45
lambda dbl 21: 42
closure add5 100: 105
counter: 1 2 3 4

--- currying: too few args returns a partial ---
((add3 1) 2) 100: 103
doubled vec: (2 4 6 8 10)
(twice inc1 5) : 7

--- recursion ---
fact 10: 3628800
fib 15 : 610
sum 1..50000 (TCO): 1250025000
even? 100 : 1
odd?  101 : 1

--- quote: code as data ---
(+ 1 2) evaluated : 3
'(+ 1 2) is data  : (+ 1 2)
'foo (a symbol)   : foo
type of '(+ 1 2)  : list
type of 'foo      : symbol

--- eval and apply ---
eval program: 10
built then eval: 60
apply add4: 10

--- meta ---
type 42        : scalar
type "hi"      : string
type 'sym      : symbol
type (list)    : list
type (vec 1 2) : vec
type square    : function
str 42         : 42
str (list 1 2) : (1 2)
num "3.14"     : 3.14

--- shared references vs explicit copy ---
orig (shared with alias): (99 2 3)
src (untouched by dup)  : (1 2 3)
dup                      : (99 2 3)

--- errors ---
num parse -> caught: reference.mu:395: num: not a number: not a number
head empty: caught: reference.mu:400: head: empty list
check 5  : 5
check -3 : reference.mu:407: negative not allowed: -3
  1> check-positive() at reference.mu:412
type error : reference.mu:415: +: expected number, got string
arity error: reference.mu:416: sqrt: expected 1 argument, got 0
size error : reference.mu:417: +: size mismatch (2 vs 3)
assert     : reference.mu:421: assertion failed: one is not two
call stack : reference.mu:424: from inner
  1> inner() at reference.mu:426
  2> outer() at reference.mu:429

--- file I/O ---
contents of /tmp/musil_demo.txt:
first line
second line
third line

exec stat:
3 /tmp/musil_demo.txt

--- load ---
(see comment in source — load "file.mu" pulls in another .mu;
 loaded files are cached so cycles and double-loads are safe)

--- closing: Newton's method for sqrt ---
newton sqrt 2   : 1.41421356237309
newton sqrt 612 : 24.738633753706
math   sqrt 612 : 24.738633753706
newton on vector: (1 2 3 4 5)

================================================================
  end of reference
================================================================
